---
import HubLayout from "../../../layouts/HubLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../../../data/site";
---

<HubLayout
  title="VTC Rules"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { label: "Home", href: "/hub/" },
    { label: "Training", href: "/hub/training/vtc-rules" },
    { label: "VTC Rules" }
  ]}
>
  <article class="hub-panel max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="hub-page-title bg-gradient-to-r from-cyan-300 to-blue-400 bg-clip-text text-transparent">
      VTC rules
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate-300">
      Official rules and expectations for every {siteConfig.name} driver.
    </p>

    <ol class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-slate-300">
      <li class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-[#081638]/50 p-5 sm:p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">Company tag &amp; colours on TruckersMP</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          When playing on TMP, you must use the <strong class="text-white">"{siteConfig.name}"</strong> Player tag and
          use the company truck/trailer colours.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          If you're using a truck that does not have the correct paint job, please switch to one that does. More
          information on this can be found in{" "}
          <a
            href="/hub/training/getting-started"
            class="font-semibold text-cyan-300 underline decoration-cyan-400/40 underline-offset-2 transition hover:text-cyan-200"
          >
            Getting Started
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-[#081638]/50 p-5 sm:p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">Job statistics</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          The tampering of job statistics is prohibited. Altering of job distance or income, via the use of mods,
          programs, or anything of the sort, is not permissible. You must temporarily disable Trucky Job Tracking
          should you wish to do so.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          It should be noted that only TruckersMP Dispatcher are exemptions to this rule. However TruckersMP Dispatcher
          are only permitted, providing the <strong class="text-white">urgency</strong> figure is always set to{" "}
          <strong class="text-white">0</strong>. Jobs over a certain threshold will automatically be cancelled pending
          investigation from the Human Resources Team.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-[#081638]/50 p-5 sm:p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">Bans &amp; leaving the VTC</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          A member of the Driver Relations (DR) Team must be informed if you have been banned from TruckersMP, or if
          you wish to leave the VTC.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          You must notify DR via{" "}
          <a
            href={siteConfig.discordInvite}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
            class="font-semibold text-cyan-300 underline decoration-cyan-400/40 underline-offset-2 transition hover:text-cyan-200"
          >
            the support channel
          </a>
          , if you receive a ban from the TruckersMP platform, within{" "}
          <strong class="text-white">five days (120 hours)</strong> from the time the ban was issued. Failure to
          notify DR about your ban may result in stricter sanctions being applied, which could result in dismissal.
          Additionally, leaving the Discord server and/or TruckersMP VTC unannounced, and failing to rejoin within{" "}
          <strong class="text-white">24 hours</strong> of HR contacting you, will result in a permanent blacklist from{" "}
          {siteConfig.name}.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-[#081638]/50 p-5 sm:p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">Multi-clanning</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">
          The act of “multi-clanning” is fully condemned. You must not be a driver for any other Virtual Trucking
          Company, or any other group which specialises in Euro Truck Simulator 2 whilst being a driver for{" "}
          {siteConfig.name}. Exceptions can be made for drivers who wish to help out in the role of Convoy Control,
          Media, or similar, for another organisation — as long as said drivers are not logging jobs for the company.
          Permission must be granted by the Driver Relations Team in order to take on extra responsibilities in another
          organisation, similar to those mentioned above.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </article>
</HubLayout>
